      "writtenOn": "2022-08-17T13:15:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Really digging into the issue gave me new appreciation for the subtleties of skbug.com/8791 and why real GLSL doesn\u0027t have flexible literal types. The only way to fix the issue (AFAICS) would be for the outer assignment-expression to influence the type of the inner FunctionCall-expression, and it\u0027s not clear how to implement something like that with what we have today, where expressions don\u0027t have any knowledge of their neighbors.",
